WEBVTT

00:01.180 --> 00:03.230
We're going home, Shiori.

00:03.890 --> 00:06.370
M-M...

00:06.930 --> 00:08.710
Mother?!

00:08.710 --> 00:10.520
"Mother"?!

00:13.800 --> 00:17.200
Good evening. I am Shiori's father.

00:17.200 --> 00:18.540
I am her mother.

00:19.170 --> 00:21.260
Are you a friend of Shiori's?

00:21.260 --> 00:25.780
N-Nice to meet you! I'm Kuga, 
I spoke to you over the phone.

00:26.400 --> 00:28.040
That was you?

00:31.420 --> 00:33.970
<b>Princess</b>

00:31.920 --> 00:33.130
Word up.

00:33.130 --> 00:33.920
Yeah!

00:36.460 --> 00:38.860
Somehow, I pictured him differently.

00:39.530 --> 00:41.550
A-Anyway...

00:45.190 --> 00:46.850
I-I'm sorry!

00:48.330 --> 00:50.810
Well, is this your family?

00:52.050 --> 00:53.810
My sister and brother.

00:59.500 --> 01:02.020
Sorry to show up unannounced.

01:02.020 --> 01:04.210
It must be bedtime for the children.

01:04.730 --> 01:06.470
I'm sorry, too,

01:06.470 --> 01:09.760
for speaking to you over the 
phone the way I did.

01:11.850 --> 01:13.540
We should reapproach this.

01:13.540 --> 01:15.720
Could you spare some time tomorrow?

01:15.720 --> 01:17.390
O-Of course.

01:17.700 --> 01:18.470
Right?

01:22.450 --> 01:24.460
See you tomorrow, then.

01:30.440 --> 01:33.970
I'm sorry. That must have frightened you.

01:33.970 --> 01:36.240
No, I'm fine.

01:37.930 --> 01:40.500
Fine, everything's fine.

01:41.900 --> 01:44.000
I-It <i>is</i> fine!

01:44.000 --> 01:45.550
We'll talk it all out!

01:56.220 --> 02:03.510
Looks like it started before I knew it

02:04.260 --> 02:09.310
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

02:11.230 --> 02:19.280
The usual townscape lends 
charm to the two of us

02:19.280 --> 02:24.790
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

02:28.540 --> 02:30.620
Suddenly buying flowers

02:30.620 --> 02:32.630
Standing around in the kitchen

02:32.630 --> 02:35.840
Sending a photo, because 
the setting sun is pretty

02:35.840 --> 02:40.380
Trying to spend as much 
time with you as I can

02:40.380 --> 02:43.390
This is all new for me

02:45.260 --> 02:50.940
I hope tomorrow is like today

02:51.270 --> 02:57.480
I've never felt this way before

02:57.480 --> 03:03.070
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

03:03.740 --> 03:09.000
But it's fine if we stay home

03:10.250 --> 03:13.460
I can't wait to see you

03:15.960 --> 03:20.970
<b><b>Episode 10</b></b>

03:15.960 --> 03:20.970
<b>Family Meeting</b>

03:15.960 --> 03:20.970
<b><b>with the Princess</b></b>

03:23.810 --> 03:25.960
I'm <i>not</i> going back, and that's final!

03:25.960 --> 03:28.730
Yeah, this is tricky.

03:29.450 --> 03:32.480
You must give Shiori her freedom.

03:33.230 --> 03:35.720
Well, there's my grandmother's dying wish,

03:35.720 --> 03:38.410
so I don't think there's 
any forcing me to go.

03:38.410 --> 03:40.730
It holds that much sway?

03:40.730 --> 03:41.760
Yes.

03:44.740 --> 03:49.480
What worries me is that they might 
do something to your family.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.680
I-I don't think that'll happen.

03:52.680 --> 03:55.210
They showed concern for Machi and Fumio.

03:55.210 --> 03:58.240
Also, this could be our chance.

04:00.690 --> 04:03.230
If we're going to annul the Engagement Pact,

04:03.230 --> 04:06.250
the ones who're most likely 
to know how are here.

04:09.370 --> 04:10.760
That's true.

04:12.110 --> 04:16.050
By the way, who's the one 
you asked to look into it?

04:16.050 --> 04:17.780
She came along with them.

04:24.260 --> 04:27.410
I wonder if your parents know 
I'm in the pact with you.

04:27.410 --> 04:33.650
No, the way they acted, I doubt they 
know you ever touched my stinger.

04:33.950 --> 04:35.220
Okay.

04:35.220 --> 04:37.890
Anyway, knowing how my mother thinks,

04:37.890 --> 04:42.170
if we bring up canceling the pact, 
she'll see it as us breaking up.

04:42.170 --> 04:44.430
So, we deceive them?

04:45.330 --> 04:51.370
Kuga-san, there are people in this 
world with whom there is no reasoning.

04:51.370 --> 04:53.930
A-All right.

04:54.340 --> 04:58.670
Listen, we'll ask how to annul the pact.

04:58.670 --> 05:01.100
Then, we'll have them leave in peace.

05:02.360 --> 05:04.480
Those are tomorrow's objectives.

05:18.060 --> 05:21.330
<i>I am the princess of the Star People.</i>

05:23.630 --> 05:25.380
<i>The time has finally come.</i>

05:25.990 --> 05:28.740
<i>Here's hoping we can settle 
things peacefully.</i>

05:32.220 --> 05:35.230
Modest

05:32.220 --> 05:35.230
Blushes when
complimented

05:37.570 --> 05:41.030
<i>I hope things go well tomorrow.</i>

05:45.210 --> 05:49.230
Sorry to ask, Chibi-chan, but please
look after Machi and Fumio.

05:49.230 --> 05:51.230
Sure. See you later.

05:51.740 --> 05:53.740
Okay, we'll be back.

05:53.980 --> 05:55.740
Good luck!

05:55.740 --> 05:56.740
Luck!

05:58.750 --> 06:03.250
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

06:00.970 --> 06:02.220
See you later.

06:05.950 --> 06:07.600
I wonder if they'll be okay.

06:07.600 --> 06:08.930
I'm nervous.

06:08.930 --> 06:10.680
I'm sure they'll be fine.

06:28.860 --> 06:29.780
Hi.

06:32.110 --> 06:34.050
H-Hello.

06:34.050 --> 06:35.760
I'm glad you came.

06:38.410 --> 06:39.800
Where are the other two?

06:39.800 --> 06:44.290
Waiting in the room.
 Today's an important family-only affair.

06:44.540 --> 06:49.750
I-I'm thinking a fresh start and 
a good conversation will help.

06:50.380 --> 06:52.720
There is nothing to discuss with you.

06:55.890 --> 06:58.500
Nor do we need to know anything about you.

07:00.330 --> 07:03.270
Because your relationship 
is out of the question.

07:08.440 --> 07:11.020
You really are rude, Mother.

07:11.020 --> 07:14.570
You're only allowed to behave 
that way on the island.

07:14.570 --> 07:17.580
There are no rude people on the island.

07:21.490 --> 07:23.570
Both of you, calm down.

07:28.980 --> 07:32.580
Don't worry about me.
 Focus on the objectives.

07:38.480 --> 07:41.070
There's something I want 
the two of you to know.

07:41.970 --> 07:44.690
About the Engagement Pact.

07:44.690 --> 07:48.440
Let's emphasize that you touched the 
stinger while trying to help me.

07:52.170 --> 07:57.860
I wrote about what wonderful a person 
Kuga-san is, so please start by looking at this.

07:59.690 --> 08:00.720
Wait!

08:01.250 --> 08:02.370
Why?

08:03.330 --> 08:06.930
It's going to seem a little suspicious, 
so let's pass on that for now.

08:06.930 --> 08:10.370
But this is necessary in order to explain.

08:10.370 --> 08:14.510
Regardless of how you feel, 
it's superficial in the end.

08:15.900 --> 08:19.510
Kuga-san does not know who we truly are.

08:20.270 --> 08:23.650
If an outsider knew what would 
happen if he were joined with you,

08:23.920 --> 08:27.080
he would turn tail and run.

08:28.460 --> 08:29.750
He is no exception.

08:30.380 --> 08:35.910
Even so, Kuga-san knows about my 
background and he still accepts me!

08:39.670 --> 08:41.590
Accepts you?

08:42.090 --> 08:45.160
Um, we'll explain things in order!

08:45.160 --> 08:46.540
Don't tell me...

08:47.510 --> 08:51.170
You blabbed about your 
true identity to an outsider?!

08:51.390 --> 08:55.520
For the record, it was only by 
accident that he got stung!

08:55.930 --> 08:57.050
Stung?!

08:58.310 --> 09:00.310
Like she said, an accident!

09:00.310 --> 09:03.300
It's on her... backside, you know!

09:03.840 --> 09:07.140
You know how sacred your stinger is.

09:08.170 --> 09:09.940
How could you be so immoral?!

09:09.940 --> 09:12.670
W-We still haven't gone that far!

09:12.670 --> 09:14.710
It's true! It was an accident!

09:15.260 --> 09:17.700
You expect me to believe such an excuse?

09:21.710 --> 09:25.400
Y-You're the partner in her Engagement Pact?

09:26.160 --> 09:28.840
Shiori is the princess of the Star People.

09:28.840 --> 09:32.410
A Star Child who will someday 
reign over her people as queen.

09:32.890 --> 09:36.310
Someone not of the island 
has no right to touch her.

09:38.020 --> 09:43.800
My poor daughter. You've been 
taken in by a ne'er-do-well.

09:53.390 --> 09:57.500
You never put any faith in me.

09:58.040 --> 09:59.460
Enough of this!

10:02.320 --> 10:03.520
Goshiki-san!

10:03.520 --> 10:04.570
Shiori!

10:04.570 --> 10:05.870
Come back here!

10:07.370 --> 10:08.550
Shiori!

10:21.700 --> 10:23.850
Mother!

10:24.040 --> 10:28.580
I'm the fastest runner in the lower grades!

10:28.580 --> 10:31.360
Nobody can ever catch up to me!

10:31.630 --> 10:32.690
Oh?

10:33.890 --> 10:36.440
I also got first place on field day.

10:36.440 --> 10:39.100
May I go play tag with everyone?

10:39.320 --> 10:42.800
Shiori, what if you got hurt?

10:42.800 --> 10:46.480
Besides, I'm sure you'd never be "it" in tag.

10:47.090 --> 10:50.440
Are you trying to say they 
all lose on purpose?

10:50.440 --> 10:51.570
No.

10:52.820 --> 10:57.500
You can do anything. 
You are a wonderful person.

10:57.780 --> 11:00.500
But you are a Star Child.

11:00.500 --> 11:04.510
For everyone here, that 
makes you irreplaceable.

11:04.820 --> 11:08.520
So, be a good girl and go play in the house.

11:08.520 --> 11:09.640
All right?

11:10.660 --> 11:11.540
Yes, ma'am.

11:25.920 --> 11:29.920
I'm sorry. So much for striving 
towards those objectives.

11:31.480 --> 11:32.560
Yeah.

11:32.560 --> 11:35.490
Well, all that was... not easy, huh?

11:36.430 --> 11:37.300
Here.

11:38.300 --> 11:40.010
Thank you.

11:42.940 --> 11:51.680
I'm not on speaking terms with my 
own mother, so I know how you feel.

11:52.770 --> 11:58.200
But I mean, sometimes I do wish 
she and I had a decent relationship.

11:59.720 --> 12:00.940
What about you?

12:01.760 --> 12:06.950
Well for starters, it'd be 
nice if I introduced you,

12:08.260 --> 12:12.490
and they were happy I have a good boyfriend.

12:17.680 --> 12:19.160
Hey!

12:22.080 --> 12:23.280
Everything okay?

12:23.280 --> 12:24.340
Yes.

12:24.340 --> 12:27.340
Uh, is it okay for you two to be apart?

12:27.340 --> 12:29.940
Oh, you mean that?

12:29.940 --> 12:33.240
Right, right. You're in a pact, too.

12:33.240 --> 12:35.480
You know about what happens.

12:35.480 --> 12:37.400
Right.

12:38.090 --> 12:39.760
I'm fine.

12:39.760 --> 12:42.860
Let's head back. Miyako's waiting.

12:42.860 --> 12:43.950
All right.

12:53.060 --> 12:54.800
I know...

12:55.240 --> 12:59.760
you would never thoughtlessly 
yield yourself to another.

13:01.000 --> 13:02.790
I apologize for what I said.

13:07.270 --> 13:08.120
All right.

13:10.520 --> 13:11.750
What accident?

13:12.190 --> 13:13.960
Please let me explain!

13:17.430 --> 13:21.770
I see, you claim you were 
trying to help her.

13:26.270 --> 13:31.580
Even if you're trying to take responsibility, 
this relationship is still meaningless!

13:31.580 --> 13:34.290
The engagement is to be 
annulled immediately!

13:34.570 --> 13:35.400
Yes!

13:40.930 --> 13:41.800
Huh?

13:41.800 --> 13:43.430
We'll annul it.

13:43.960 --> 13:45.390
You will?

13:45.390 --> 13:46.550
We will.

13:48.550 --> 13:49.430
<b>annulment</b>

13:49.430 --> 13:50.300
<b>annulment</b>

13:50.300 --> 13:51.560
<b> break-up</b>

13:50.300 --> 13:51.560
<b>annulment</b>

13:52.880 --> 13:53.760
I...

13:55.010 --> 13:57.460
I finally got through to you!

13:59.870 --> 14:00.950
Yes.

14:02.080 --> 14:03.410
In return...

14:04.720 --> 14:07.230
There are still things I want to do here.

14:07.230 --> 14:11.750
Well! Something similar might happen again!

14:12.140 --> 14:13.240
I am against it!

14:14.670 --> 14:19.000
Per the previous generation's 
dying wish, I am free.

14:19.000 --> 14:21.150
She's gone now.

14:21.150 --> 14:24.670
What you want to do... Manga, was it?

14:25.040 --> 14:27.750
Have you accomplished 
anything these past months?

14:30.260 --> 14:33.510
Have you drawn anything that anyone values?

14:34.420 --> 14:37.010
W-Well...

14:37.900 --> 14:43.900
Kuga-san, you know that we are the 
guarantors on Shiori's lease, correct?

14:43.900 --> 14:46.680
Her father is, yes.

14:48.020 --> 14:51.560
She's free, only with our financial support?

14:51.560 --> 14:54.280
Yet there she sits, 
enjoying every minute of it.

14:54.520 --> 14:57.780
Your lifestyle here will render you useless.

14:59.590 --> 15:00.720
Excuse me.

15:01.580 --> 15:04.040
What's wrong with her enjoying herself?

15:08.530 --> 15:11.860
Uh, I mean, she's better at 
communicating than I am.

15:11.860 --> 15:15.550
And she actively tries 
to engage with others.

15:16.250 --> 15:19.450
She became friends with
 my brother and sister.

15:20.260 --> 15:25.050
Also, she was nice enough to write welcome 
letters to everyone when she moved in.

15:25.460 --> 15:30.110
She made a fortune-telling booth and 
outfit using things we had on hand.

15:31.620 --> 15:32.660
Fortune-telling?

15:32.660 --> 15:38.680
What I mean is: Things some would think are
 too much effort or not worth the trouble...

15:39.820 --> 15:45.070
and other everyday things people forget,
 she enjoys spotting those and acting on them.

15:45.520 --> 15:48.150
To me, she seems downright radiant.

15:55.720 --> 15:58.720
Also, she <i>has</i> been working.

15:59.330 --> 16:00.960
Working?

16:01.770 --> 16:03.970
I brought these along.

16:04.760 --> 16:08.830
Goshiki-san did all the backgrounds 
and treatments on these.

16:14.580 --> 16:17.840
Kuga-san, they won't understand.

16:17.840 --> 16:21.380
They've never read any manga.

16:21.760 --> 16:25.460
These are art samples I got from 
her to use as reference materials,

16:25.460 --> 16:28.500
and this is work she did for another artist.

16:28.820 --> 16:30.510
Another artist?

16:30.860 --> 16:33.480
Oh, I drew this one.

16:31.470 --> 16:34.260
Alice and the Knight of Thorns
<b>Momo-Tea Kokone</b>

16:34.260 --> 16:40.020
<b>Momo-Tea Kokone</b>

16:34.260 --> 16:40.020
<b>Momo-Tea Kokone</b>

16:35.040 --> 16:37.170
It's a different name.

16:37.760 --> 16:40.820
It's a pen name. That is...

16:40.820 --> 16:42.760
I am Momo-Tea Kokone!

16:44.160 --> 16:46.840
I-It's okay if you don't 
understand right now!

16:46.840 --> 16:49.830
Like, how to read manga, 
or how good the art is!

16:54.180 --> 16:57.070
She's working hard, and I'm 
not demanding your approval!

16:57.070 --> 17:02.980
But I won't let you say these 
past months have been for nothing!

17:06.600 --> 17:09.910
Of course, I understand that you're worried.

17:09.910 --> 17:14.050
I'd be a nervous wreck
 if my sister or brother left home.

17:15.530 --> 17:18.930
But please...

17:18.930 --> 17:20.680
Could you give her time?

17:29.510 --> 17:32.000
How about we try it for a year?

17:32.410 --> 17:35.080
And we'll lower your allowance a bit,

17:35.410 --> 17:38.270
so you can attempt to 
really support yourself.

17:39.120 --> 17:42.590
Will you support her so there 
are no mishaps, Kuga-san?

17:42.860 --> 17:45.070
Yes! Of course!

17:46.580 --> 17:47.840
How about it?

17:48.360 --> 17:50.580
A new vow?

17:51.220 --> 17:54.140
We'll give you another year, then.

17:56.950 --> 18:00.180
We'll come and get you one year from now.

18:03.130 --> 18:06.010
Thank you, Mother.

18:07.860 --> 18:10.090
For now, that's enough.

18:13.500 --> 18:15.020
Oh, yes.

18:15.020 --> 18:18.800
We don't know any details about 
annulling the pact, either.

18:19.370 --> 18:23.150
When we get back to the island,
 I'll send you documents that describe how.

18:23.670 --> 18:26.260
Thank you for helping us.

18:27.190 --> 18:29.730
It doesn't mean I'm on your side, though.

18:32.420 --> 18:35.850
The person I most want to support is Miyako.

18:35.850 --> 18:38.250
Manga can be drawn on the island too, can't it?

18:39.460 --> 18:40.470
Yes...

18:47.680 --> 18:49.910
I'm glad you're doing well.

18:55.590 --> 18:57.410
Until next time.

19:04.810 --> 19:08.180
I-It's over.

19:08.730 --> 19:12.050
Accepting lopsided affection is exhausting.

19:15.660 --> 19:18.930
Why do you end up losing 
confidence, Kuga-san?

19:19.160 --> 19:24.150
I don't want the one I love 
to look down on himself!

19:26.620 --> 19:30.510
My wanting you to have 
confidence in yourself.

19:30.510 --> 19:33.180
And my wanting you to be happy as a result.

19:33.180 --> 19:34.560
That was pushy of me.

19:34.880 --> 19:37.790
I don't think this and 
that are the same thing.

19:38.830 --> 19:41.200
No, yeah...

19:41.950 --> 19:46.380
Sorry I can't respond right away, 
when you've shared so much with me.

19:47.440 --> 19:52.810
It's like it's a present I can't open,
 because it's too good for me.

19:55.580 --> 19:58.220
Well then, that means it's still there.

20:04.780 --> 20:07.640
Thank you for holding on to it for me.

20:08.900 --> 20:12.980
Thanks for being by my side today.

20:17.780 --> 20:19.210
Let's head home.

20:22.650 --> 20:24.360
I'm worried.

20:24.370 --> 20:26.240
<b>Zoopedia</b>

20:26.470 --> 20:28.380
They're taking so long.

20:32.660 --> 20:34.880
I'm going to the kitchen. 
Want anything to drink?

20:35.960 --> 20:38.120
No, but thanks.

20:47.850 --> 20:50.890
The "relax and take it easy" color came up.

20:51.230 --> 20:52.570
Easy.

20:55.850 --> 20:58.510
Shio-chan should just join our family.

21:00.990 --> 21:04.670
Does that means we'd have not just 
a big brother, but a big sister, too?!

21:05.080 --> 21:06.690
That'd be sweet!

21:08.020 --> 21:09.360
Let's make a prayer!

21:11.190 --> 21:12.400
Here goes!

21:14.680 --> 21:18.730
<i>I've never seen a shooting star, 
so we'll just make one of our own.</i>

21:19.700 --> 21:21.770
<i>May Shio-chan always be with us.</i>

21:24.200 --> 21:28.440
May we cheer up! May we 
cheer up! May we cheer up!

21:32.320 --> 21:36.980
It's fine. Fortune-telling and 
magic words shouldn't be too strong.

21:36.980 --> 21:37.710
Yeah.

21:38.740 --> 21:41.790
<i>I'm sure my wish will come true.</i>

21:44.570 --> 21:46.230
They're back!

21:46.230 --> 21:47.300
Back!

21:51.750 --> 21:52.970
How did it go?

21:53.210 --> 21:56.710
It went well, one way or another.

21:57.290 --> 21:59.620
Yes, that it did.

21:59.940 --> 22:01.670
Good!

22:01.670 --> 22:03.070
Good, good.

22:03.070 --> 22:04.450
I'm glad.

22:16.060 --> 22:27.650
A long red thread stretching 
into the distance

22:27.650 --> 22:38.800
Meeting you, even if it meant having 
to cross hundreds of light-years

22:38.800 --> 22:45.480
Maybe I'll slowly get used to

22:45.480 --> 22:52.390
The two of us going out to have fun

22:52.390 --> 23:02.230
A tug on my arm, by the bond 
that was formed that day

23:02.230 --> 23:08.090
A little at a time, we've 
come closer together

23:08.090 --> 23:12.880
More smiles for us

23:12.880 --> 23:25.690
That place I first learned of, and 
the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:25.690 --> 23:31.650
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:31.650 --> 23:38.490
Looking forward to it, good night

23:45.960 --> 23:50.450
It's finally arrived, the day 
I annul my pact with Goshiki-san.

23:50.780 --> 23:53.360
But if we pull out the stinger...

23:53.360 --> 23:55.150
How will Kuga-san feel...

23:55.150 --> 23:57.040
How will Goshiki-san feel...

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b>Episode 11</b>

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b><b>Stinger Removal with Kuga-kun</b></b>

23:57.040 --> 23:58.780
...once it's gone?
